            <ArticleTitle>Efficacy of systolic vs diastolic pulsation beyond severe coronary stenosis flow.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>205-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper describes the superiority of systolic pulsatile selective coronary perfusion as compared to diastolic pulsatile coronary perfusion in improving flow beyond ischemia-producing coronary artery obstructions in the working heart. The practical implications for use in coronary support perfusion systems are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
